From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] advapi32: ACL evaluation, trustee wrappers, GetSecurityInfoEx, audit alarm A forms (3734)

advapi32: ACL evaluation, trustee wrappers, GetSecurityInfoEx, audit alarm A forms

GetEffectiveRightsFromAcl and GetAuditedPermissionsFromAcl evaluate the ACL
for a trustee (name, SID or objects-and-SID/name form): allow and deny ACEs in
order, Everyone applies to everybody, inherit-only ACEs are skipped, an
inherited deny ACE makes the ACL invalid (documented). BuildSecurityDescriptorA
converts its trustees and entries and calls the W function. The audit alarm A
forms (ObjectOpen/Close/Privilege/PrivilegedService) convert their strings and
call the W functions. LookupSecurityDescriptorParts(A/W) return the owner,
group and the DACL and SACL entries with their trustees named.
GetSecurityInfoEx and GetNamedSecurityInfoEx (A/W) fill ACTRL_ACCESS /
ACTRL_AUDIT lists and account names for the Windows provider (others give
ERROR_BAD_PROVIDER). WmiOpenBlock answers ERROR_WMI_GUID_NOT_FOUND.

Rebased at integration (integ-2026-10) onto earlier integration patches: clean 3-way merge.
